  "articleBody": "A kitchen expansion is easiest to manage when you first document the existing space, define how the added area will be used, test the proposed layout, confirm permit needs, and compare complete proposals. The finished plan should show the new footprint, structural changes, utility locations, materials, responsibilities, and inspection steps before construction starts.",
